{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}]},{"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins","anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Core Middleware","anchor":"Core-Middleware"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"action-agnostic infrastructure"}]},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"text":" so it can snapshot and compare.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Domain Plugins","anchor":"Domain-Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}]},{"code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Importing at call sites","anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"separate library target"}]},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":", but that re-exports "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"core Swidux only"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.killswitch.*"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"that"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxAnalytics"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxPaywall"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".ui(...)"},{"text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The easy case to forget is a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that reads the slice for display — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:"}]},{"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is to add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Swidux<Plugin>"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Comparison","anchor":"Comparison"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Action knowledge","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"State coupling","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Decision Rule","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"Important","style":"important"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Hook Selection Guide","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce(state:action:)"}]},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Handle domain-specific actions "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"afterReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Observe state "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"flush() async","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Registration Order","anchor":"Registration-Order"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}]},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdictReceived"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded"},{"type":"text","text":" — fires on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}]},{"type":"text","text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — or a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derived from it — instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshot, then writes back via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"type":"text","text":". For a leaf slice that write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a plain assignment whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" setter equality-gates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-diffing consumer such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observers without any extra reducer logic."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Next Steps","anchor":"Next-Steps"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},{"type":"text","text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},{"type":"text","text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Plugin Architecture"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation","title":"Explanation"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"type":"topic","title":"Security Posture","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one."}],"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Swidux","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"title":"SwiduxPlugin","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"title":"Undo \/ Redo","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"title":"Design Principles","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"title":"Architecture & Performance","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"abstract":[{"text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"title":"Store","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"title":"Persistence Middleware","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"type":"topic","title":"PluginHost","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","kind":"symbol","title":"UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin"}}}